                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Very whimsical, the absurdity of it alone makes it enjoyable for at least a short while. \nThe controls, hitboxes, etc, are of course, very much not good, but they become easy enough to manage as you play.\n\nThe levels themselves are suprisingly fun. It's not always immidiately clear how you're supposed to get through, and it's fun to figure it out.\nOther levels are very repetitive and rhythm based, which is fun in its own right.It's fairly difficult, though I imagine anyone confident in their mechanical skills could beat it just fine.\n\nThe difficulty curve is also suprisingly natual. The earlier levels though overwhelming at first do a good job teaching you what kind of mindset you should have to beat the later levels.\n\nThe music is fairly basic, but quite groovy and enjoyable. Fits the strange oil sea with flying sharks and barrels oddly well. \n\nAnd I mean, the game is free. There's really no reason not to at least open the game and laugh at the absurdity of it all.\nEven if it costed a few, If it costs less than my drink then there's nothing to be upset about",
